      },
      "privateNotes": "<p><strong>@UUID[Compendium.points-of-interest.journals.JournalEntry.jxn9bB1XhZTRpF65.JournalEntryPage.94wLkbfz0zc6czXz]{05. The Ossuary Wall}.</strong> Dead antiquarian and field sketcher. Stat block as in life, without the gear left in the camp; the Skulltaker actor holds the statistics the wall fights with. NPC Core Obsessive Researcher.</p>",
      "publicNotes": "<p>Academia rewards specialization, and so the universities and athenaeums of the Inner Sea are full to the brim of sunlight-deprived scholars who are the world experts in such obscure topics such as the migratory habits of bogwids or the folklore of pre-Choral Brevoy.</p><hr /><p>True power comes from knowledge—the power to shape the growth of kingdoms by mere whispers, stay three steps ahead of adversaries, or even know which flora is best for creating untraceable poisons.</p>\n<h2>Appearance</h2>\n<p>In life: a young field sketcher with a smudged charcoal pencil and a wide-brimmed hat. In death: a small white skull with charcoal smudges still on the brow.</p>",
      "publication": {
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true,
        "title": "Pathfinder NPC Core"
      }
